{"assets":["/editorial-assets/5b92b763c2fbf92e65dbe8d8d03cfc81c83b8ddfe1aa79a2f34e5cff36dce53e.png","/editorial-assets/430018dfca88f1022ad7d3b96b08e5aaf2d33cc4bcd7ee6dbea84975511b393e.png","/editorial-assets/b432c23d334e09047956d9416408ed84e7b9667078e9ccc415a7466093cfb2a5.png","/editorial-assets/66e459b29a71d426b10e47b75d8701355f932569174e7befa469970f76b3eda6.png","/editorial-assets/47215300bf3e37fa26a504448894d3975fb2418d47d83856e4d3f569dc819fce.png","/editorial-assets/ba80b3fb781d70f86df9a9c0d2c55a424714a147c2d566c487739d358898a4f5.png","/editorial-assets/f1e59b2c0234aab16dfd07f76c3e041c14c8e842836fd35b84be74217d0eedfd.png","/editorial-assets/f10663ebde118f0f7951dedd073bf33dd1a98700f46b56c5eb4a33834ad00045.png","/editorial-assets/d9f1727146061d1fb77d27195eae74df00f17250cc84b3ffc8835ef79f7edca9.png","/editorial-assets/d414ac8cf1c7f87bb879d34b62351ad455c6bb19eee0d8172c9be2d4c1ba129b.png","/editorial-assets/0f952d7b08f43fd122fbc2c005d3c259580df752a87cd753a7d81424bc46d8ef.png"],"contestId":"863","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863A - Quasi-palindrome"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can check if the given is quasi-palindromic by removing all the trailing zeros and checking if resulting string is a palindrome."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863B - Kayaking"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Firstly let's learn how to split persons in pairs as if there are no single kayaks. Let there be people with weights "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Obviously, the lowest instability you can achieve is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Swapping any two elements will only make the result greater. This greedy strategy can be used to distribute all the seats."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now you need to check every pair of persons to seat in single kayaks and calculate total instability for the rest. The answer will be the minimun instabily over all pairs."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863C - 1-2-3"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Notice that there are only 9 possible patterns in this game. You can used in a following way. Simulate games till one of the patterns get repeated. Games between this pair of occurences will get you the same total outcome no matter when they are played. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let the distance between the games with the same pattern is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dif"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and index of these games are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (zero-indexed). Total score of some interval is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"score"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then the answer will be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"score"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(0, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") + "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5b92b763c2fbf92e65dbe8d8d03cfc81c83b8ddfe1aa79a2f34e5cff36dce53e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" + (("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mod"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dif"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"score"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mod"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dif"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863D - Yet Another Array Queries Problem"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One can guess from the constraits that complexity of the algorithm should be either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"qm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). And there is a solution with the second one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's try to solve the reversed problem — answer what position will some number be at after all the queries. Check the impact of some query on position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let the query be on some segment ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is outside this segment then you can skip it. Otherwise reverse will swap "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", shift will swap "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" then it will be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" instead of ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1))."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This task can be translated to the given one just by reversing the query list. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"qm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Obviously, you can also solve it with Cartesian tree online in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/430018dfca88f1022ad7d3b96b08e5aaf2d33cc4bcd7ee6dbea84975511b393e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863E - Turn Off The TV"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Firstly let's compress the moments of time. Note that storing only "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" isn't enough (consider pairs ([1, 2], [3, 4]) and ([1, 2], [4, 5])), you also should take ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now moments of time are up to 6·10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". For every moment calculate the number of segments to cover it (make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" +  = 1 and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" -  = 1 for each segment and take prefix sums over this array). Then let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pref"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the number of moments of time covered by only one segment on some prefix up to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th moment. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And finally if for some segment ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] from the input "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pref"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pref"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is 0 then you can safely delete this segment."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b432c23d334e09047956d9416408ed84e7b9667078e9ccc415a7466093cfb2a5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863F - Almost Permutation"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem can be solved with mincost maxflow approach."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's construct a following network:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Construct a vertex for every number from 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". For each of these vertices add "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" directed edges from the source to this vertex, the capacity of each edge will be 1, and the costs will be 1, 3, 5, ..., 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 (so pushing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" flow from the source to the vertex will cost exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Also construct a vertex for every index of the array. For each number make add a directed edge with capacity 1 and cost 0 to every position in the array such that this number can be put into this position, and for every index make a directed edge from the vertex constructed for this index to the sink with capacity 1 and cost 0. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Minimum cost maximum flow in this network will construct a suitable array with minimum cost, so the answer to the problem is minimum cost of maximum flow in the network."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"863G"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/863/problem/G"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"863G - Graphic Settings"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1, then everything is simple. Cycle exists if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1] = 2, and path exists if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1] = 1 or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1]."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the case when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2. Let's call the combination odd if the sum of parameters is odd for this combination, and even otherwise. It's easy to see that if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1] and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[2] are both odd, then it's impossible to construct a cycle because the number of even combinations is greater than the number of odd combinations. Furthermore, it's impossible to construct a path if our initial combination is an odd one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's show how to construct answer in all other cases. Constructing a cycle is easy if at least one of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] is even:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/66e459b29a71d426b10e47b75d8701355f932569174e7befa469970f76b3eda6.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And constructing a path can be divided into four cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Starting point in corner:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/47215300bf3e37fa26a504448894d3975fb2418d47d83856e4d3f569dc819fce.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Start near the border:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ba80b3fb781d70f86df9a9c0d2c55a424714a147c2d566c487739d358898a4f5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Both coordinates of starting point are even:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f1e59b2c0234aab16dfd07f76c3e041c14c8e842836fd35b84be74217d0eedfd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Both coordinates are odd:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f10663ebde118f0f7951dedd073bf33dd1a98700f46b56c5eb4a33834ad00045.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the case when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2 is solved."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 3, then it can be reduced to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2 as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose we have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1] = 3, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[2] = 3, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[3] = 3. Then let's at first consider only combinations where the third parameter is equal to 1:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d9f1727146061d1fb77d27195eae74df00f17250cc84b3ffc8835ef79f7edca9.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, if we need to add the combinations with third parameter equal to 2, we mirror the \"layer\":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d414ac8cf1c7f87bb879d34b62351ad455c6bb19eee0d8172c9be2d4c1ba129b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And if we need to add the third \"layer\", we mirror it again:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0f952d7b08f43fd122fbc2c005d3c259580df752a87cd753a7d81424bc46d8ef.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And so on."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This way can also be used to reduce "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 3 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/54708"}